      },
      "question": {
        ":question/id": "67365bc6-453f-5a19-82a4-9817c6e05a99",
        ":question/problem": "Copy and complete the table below and use it to determine which of the following is the graph of $y=x-6.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ |  |  |  |  |",
        ":question/worked-solution": "First, we fill the table. Given a value of $x,$ we can find the corresponding $y$ by substituting $x$ into the formula $y=x-6.$ Therefore,\n\n- if $x=0$ then $y=(0)-6=-6,$\n\n- if $x=1$ then $y=(1)-6=-5,$\n\n- if $x=2$ then $y=(2)-6=-4,$ and\n\n- if $x=3$ then $y=(3)-6=-3.$\n\n| $x$ | $0$ | $1$ | $2$ | $3$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $y$ | $-6$ | $-5$ | $-4$ | $-3$ |\n\nWe plot these $(x,y)$ pairs on the $xy$-plane:\n\n![](images/99/99188f2a0f8de0054a6375a88a11242bea7e4799cc17552cd9ba0dd00d5a0788.png)\n\nFinally, connecting the points gives us a straight line. This is the graph of $y=x-6.$\n\n![](images/44/44b8f095ef9aca54e6215b1b61c9fad562dd54b0f00b7e9b8e2efdd904dd83e6.png)",
        ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
